aquila-radio-astronomy (0.2.21) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Settings: OK with the receiver on Auto no longer clears the saved gain and
    sample rate.
  * Windows: Stop, or closing the window, while the node is starting now stops it.
    A receiver that sends no samples no longer holds the node.
  * Windows: closing the app no longer leaves an error in the Windows event log.
  * A table damaged by a power cut no longer stops the candidate list, the trimming
    of old rows or the lists in the app.
  * The candidate list is no longer worked out with the receiver the node is using.
  * The window keeps updating when the address of a far node is not a node.
  * RTL-SDR: the bias tee is switched off when it is set off. The test signal now
    works on RTL-SDR and HackRF.
  * Day view and 3D plot: no empty stripes at high sample rates or with scans far
    apart.
  * Smaller fixes in Settings, Quick setup, the Log tab and the sky map.

 -- Ayushman Tripathi <ayushmantripathi7724@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:48:09 -0500

aquila-radio-astronomy (0.2.20) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hydrogen line: an RTL-SDR whose band dips on both sides of its centre gave no
    calibrated plot. A dip that comes back up no longer ends the usable band.

